Ladybird merges blocking answers the way Chromium’s
MergeCancelOfResponses and MergeOnBeforeRequestResponses do: any
cancel wins, and otherwise the most recently installed extension’s
answer counts. Firefox applies listeners one after another in
WebRequest.sys.mjs, where a cancel also ends the request. A listener’s
promise is awaited as in both. A canceled request’s onErrorOccurred
reports NS_ERROR_ABORT, Firefox’s name for it.

As in Firefox, a blocking onHeadersReceived can replace Set-Cookie and
Content-Security-Policy before they take effect, since RequestServer
pauses the transfer before it stores cookies and HSTS; Chromium gets the
same through its extraHeaders option.
